					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 4: FLOAT 2 MATH\n\nIn this example we are creating a complex pattern by multiplying two Float2 collections\nThe first collection is generated by combining two Linear collections into a Float 2 collection.\nThe second collection is generated by the Circle pattern and multiplied with the first to create this weird pattern.\n\nAlso note that the Float2 type can be converted directly to a Transformation2D type for the transformation inlet of the Mesh2D note.\nWhen doing this scale and rotation will be ignored."
					}
				},
